Z||000000||2M4 Dale||04-10-2000||07:22 AM||||I have a head off an 84 Chevy Citation. Will this head fit onto my 87 Fiero ? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChadMan||04-10-2000||09:53 AM||||I'm about 98% sure it will bolt onto your block, but I don't think the '87 intake manifold will work with the 84 Citation head...<P>I'm going to have to use a lifeline.  I'd like to call...Sage.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BN Boomer||04-10-2000||01:25 PM||||Hey Dale, I have an almost complete 2.5L engine out of an 87 Coupe that I was just going to dump off at a wrecking yard. I think it is only missing one of the coil packs. It has 170,000 miles on it and a knocking rod but seemed to run okay otherwise. If you are interested, I could pull the head off and ship it to you. I saw in another thread you are an FFL dealer, maybe we could work out a trade for a NIW USGI AR15 mag or two. Let me know.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sage||04-10-2000||04:27 PM||||Chad, thanks for the vote of confidence, but I am not sure how much good I can do you, as I am not familar with the citation engine.  What I do know is that I am running a head on my 84se(that has an 87 block) from a 79 chevy monza 2.5, that everyone I asked and all the books, say will not work.  If you are going to change the head anyway, get a gasket kit and see if all the port openings and bolt holes are the same.  In order to use the head I had, the small freeze plug inside the head and the large one on the outside had to be switched to the opposite end.  Also had to grind about 1/2" off the stock fiero thermostat housing bolt flange in order for it fit flush against the casting.  Other than that, it was pretty much a straight bolt on.<P>     Anytime you can replace a 2.5 head that has the tapered "v" between the valves, with one that is just a regular oval,(combustion chamber I.e.), you are "ahead", in my opinion, as the ones with the "v" are very prone to cracking, which could lead to much bigger "headaches".<P>     I have put 15,000 trouble free miles on this engine since the head swap.  It uses the same rockers and push rods as the stock head that was taken off.  Both intake and exhaust manifolds worked fine.<BR>     Hope this helps.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000004||2M4 Dale||04-10-2000||11:47 PM||||OK guys Thanks...I got rid of the head tonight anyway...($60.00) Didn't really need it (YET) anyway. And BN Boomer I could probably get you some mags anyway. What are you looking for 30rnd.? Steel - polymer ? These things are starting to get expensive Ya know...supply is drying up. Let me know.||||reg||1
